@tradition lap-of-the-wren
// Lap of the Wren (0.60.7): a slow walk round the promenade together, chatting. The easiest tradition to join.
// Lantern walk (once a year, the same Monday evening, the same promenade) is rarer, so on its night it takes the place.
k: 442
title: Lap of the Wren
when: weekly monday
at: 20:30-21:15
min: 20
jitter: 10
where: 3 room Promenade: bench
where: 3 room Lift plaza: bench
hold: none
who: window-seat 50%, lingers-at-meals 35%, early-to-bed 10%, everyone 22%
anim: talk
from: The promenade


== mail
- Lap of the Wren at {time}: one slow walk round the promenade. No pace, no rules, just company.

== ask
- Lap of the Wren tonight? It's just walking. And gossip.   #funny
- Walk the promenade with us later? Slow as you like.

== here
- Slower, slower. It's not a race. It's a stroll.   #funny
- Look at the stars from this side. Different, isn't it?
- One lap, then tea. That's the deal.

== thanks
- You join the slow walk round the promenade. People fall into step, chat, and drift between groups as the stars slide past.

== chatter
- Lap of the Wren's the best bit of a Monday.
- I walk the lap to stretch my legs and my ears.   #funny
- Monday lap tonight. Bring someone new.
